🟢 DAY 1 — AI ROOKIE
What You’re Actually Working With
📘 Micro-learning
AI predicts patterns — accuracy depends on what you give it
● Generative AI predicts the next most likely word based on patterns
● It does not understand truth, intent, or consequence
● Accuracy depends on the quality and structure of your input
Example prompt
“Before answering, explain what information you need from me to give an accurate
response.”


❓ Micro-assessment (MCQ)
Which statement best explains how AI produces an answer?
A. It reasons like a human
B. It looks up facts
C. It predicts likely word patterns based on input ✅
D. It decides the best outcome
Coaching
● ✅ Correct: This explains why input quality matters so much.
● ❌ Not quite: AI does not reason or decide — it predicts.


🎯 Micro-action
Ask AI what information it would need to answer a task accurately.
🧾 AI Usage Log (Required)
● Category
● Tool used
● Time saved (banded)
● Output confidence: Low / Medium / High
🌡 Confidence Check
⬜ Low ⬜ Medium ⬜ High



